{"title":"Mutate a Market Inventory","lesson":"L1 · Sets and Dictionaries · Dictionary basics","desc":"Use a dictionary to track market items. Call <code>update()</code> to change the banana count and add oranges, use <code>pop()</code> to remove apples while saving their count, and use <code>del</code> to remove oranges. Then print the final inventory and removed apples.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"uses-update","label":"Uses update() to mutate the dictionary","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\.update\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"uses-pop","label":"Uses pop() to remove an item","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\.pop\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"uses-del","label":"Uses del to remove a dictionary item","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\bdel\s+","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"prints-results","label":"Prints the changed dictionary results","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"print\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Inventory: {'bananas': 8}
Removed apples: 4</code></pre>","targetSub":"The final inventory and the apples removed with pop().","files":{"guide":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"inventory = {"apples": 4, "bananas": 6}

