{"title":"Flip a Dictionary with a Loop","lesson":"L1 · Control flow — for and while · Looping idioms","desc":"A dictionary called <code>code_words</code> maps letters to words. Construct a new dictionary called <code>flipped</code> where each word becomes a key and its letter becomes the value. Use a <code>for</code> loop with <code>.items()</code>; do not use a dictionary comprehension. The values are unique, so no entries will be overwritten.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"creates-flipped-dict","label":"Creates an empty destination dictionary","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"flipped\s*=\s*\{\s*\}","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"uses-for-loop","label":"Uses a for loop","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\bfor\b","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"iterates-items","label":"Iterates through dictionary items","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\.items\s*\(\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"reverses-pair","label":"Stores each value as a key and each key as a value","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"flipped\s*\[\s*value\s*\]\s*=\s*key","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Flipped: {'apple': 'A', 'banana': 'B', 'cherry': 'C'}</code></pre>","targetSub":"The words are now keys, and the letters are their values.","files":{"guide":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"# The original dictionary maps letters to words
