{"title":"Nested Loop Time Detective","lesson":"L1 · Nested loops · Performance awareness","desc":"Write a program that counts how many times the body of a doubly-nested loop runs. Test several values of <code>n</code>, study the pattern, and print the predicted time complexity.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"defines-counter-function","label":"Defines an operation-counting function","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+count_operations\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"uses-two-loops","label":"Uses two loops over n elements","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"for\s+\w+\s+in\s+range\s*\(\s*n\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":2},{"id":"counts-inner-work","label":"Counts each inner-loop operation","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"operations\s*\+=\s*1","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"predicts-quadratic-time","label":"Predicts quadratic time complexity","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"O\s*\(\s*n\s*\^\s*2\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>n = 2, operations = 4
n = 4, operations = 16
n = 8, operations = 64
Predicted time complexity: O(n^2)</code></pre>","targetSub":"The operation count grows as n × n, so the loop is quadratic.","files":{"guide":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"def count_operations(n):
    operations = 0

    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(n):
            operations += 1

    return operations

for n in (2, 4, 8):
    print(f"n = {n}, operations = {count_operations(n)}")

print("Predicted time complexity: O(n^2)")"},"pair":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"def count_operations(n):
    operations = 0

    for i in range(n):
        # 👈 YOUR CODE: add a loop over n, count each operation, and return the total
        operations += 0

    return operations"},"solo":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":""}},"solution":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"def count_operations(n):
    operations = 0

    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(n):
            operations += 1

    return operations

for n in (2, 4, 8):
    print(f"n = {n}, operations = {count_operations(n)}")

print("Predicted time complexity: O(n^2)")"},"hints":[{"tier":"nudge","text":"The outer loop runs n times, and for every one of those runs, the inner loop also runs n times."},{"tier":"approach","text":"Count one operation inside the inner loop. Compare the results for n = 2, 4, and 8, then express n multiplied by n using Big O notation."}],"review":[{"type":"good","text":"You counted the inner-loop work and connected n repetitions of the outer loop with n repetitions of the inner loop."},{"type":"tip","text":"When two independent loops are nested, multiply their work: n × n = n², which is O(n²)."}],"guideSteps":[{"explain":"Create a function that will return the number of operations performed for a given value of n.","label":"Create the counter","code":"def count_operations(n):
    operations = 0
    return operations"},{"explain":"Put a second loop inside the first and increase the counter once for every visit to the inner loop body.","label":"Add nested loops","code":"def count_operations(n):
    operations = 0

    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(n):
            operations += 1

    return operations"},{"explain":"Test increasing values of n so you can observe that doubling n multiplies the work by four.","label":"Study the pattern","code":"def count_operations(n):
    operations = 0

    for i in range(n):
