{"title":"Find the Lowest and Highest Score","lesson":"L1 · Control flow — more with loops · Common loop idioms","desc":"Use a running-min/running-max loop to find the lowest and highest values in a list of scores. Start both running values with the first score, then visit the remaining scores and update them when needed. Do not use the built-in <code>min()</code> or <code>max()</code> functions.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"has-score-loop","label":"Loops through the scores","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\bfor\s+\w+\s+in\s+","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"initializes-bounds","label":"Initializes both running bounds","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"(running_min|running_max)\s*=\s*scores\s*\[\s*0\s*\]","flags":"i","minCount":2},{"id":"updates-lowest","label":"Updates the running minimum","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"score\s*<\s*running_min|running_min\s*=\s*score","flags":"i","minCount":2},{"id":"updates-highest","label":"Updates the running maximum","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"score\s*>\s*running_max|running_max\s*=\s*score","flags":"i","minCount":2}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Lowest score: 64
