{"title":"Compose a Museum Trip Planner","lesson":"L1 · Problem solving 3 · Function-based problem solving","desc":"Build a small museum trip planner by composing several helper functions inside a top-level <code>main()</code>. Define functions to provide ticket prices, calculate the total, create a budget message, and print the receipt. Then make <code>main()</code> call them in the correct order and run it with the standard Python entry-point guard.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"has-main-function","label":"Defines a main() function","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+main\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"has-helper-functions","label":"Defines the smaller helper functions","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+(?:get_ticket_prices|calculate_total|budget_message|print_receipt)\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":4},{"id":"main-orchestrates-functions","label":"Passes data through the helper functions in main()","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"(?:prices\s*=\s*get_ticket_prices\s*\(|total\s*=\s*calculate_total\s*\(|message\s*=\s*budget_message\s*\(|print_receipt\s*\(\s*len\s*\()","flags":"i","minCount":4},{"id":"has-entry-point-guard","label":"Calls main() through the Python entry-point guard","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"if\s+__name__\s*==\s*["']__main__["']","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Museum trip
Visitors: 4
Total: $29.00
Within budget: yes!</code></pre>","targetSub":"A composed museum trip receipt with the total budget check.","files":{"guide":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"def get_ticket_prices():
    return [8.50, 8.50, 6.00, 6.00]


def calculate_total(prices):
    return sum(prices)


def budget_message(total, budget):
    if total <= budget:
        return "Within budget: yes!"
    return "Within budget: no!"


def print_receipt(visitor_count, total, message):
    print("Museum trip")
    print(f"Visitors: {visitor_count}")
    print(f"Total: ${total:.2f}")
    print(message)


def main():
    prices = get_ticket_prices()
    total = calculate_total(prices)
    budget = 30.00
