{"title":"Rescue the Score Checker","lesson":"Python · Errors and exceptions · Raising exceptions","desc":"Debug a score checker that crashes when the user enters text or a score outside the valid range. Add the correct <code>ValueError</code> exception handler so invalid input receives a friendly message, while valid scores still print either <code>Pass</code> or <code>Retry</code>.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"uses-try-block","label":"Adds a try block","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"try\s*:","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"catches-value-error","label":"Catches ValueError","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"except\s+ValueError\s*:","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"raises-value-error","label":"Validates the score with ValueError","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"raise\s+ValueError","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"prints-invalid-message","label":"Prints a friendly invalid-input message","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"Invalid\s+score","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Enter a score from 0 to 100: abc
