{"title":"Car Has an Engine, Car Is a Vehicle","lesson":"L1 · Object-Oriented Programming 1 · OOP design","desc":"Create a small Python model that shows the difference between <strong>inheritance</strong> and <strong>composition</strong>. A <code>Car</code> is a <code>Vehicle</code>, so it inherits from <code>Vehicle</code>. A <code>Car</code> has an <code>Engine</code>, so it stores an <code>Engine</code> object inside itself. Print checks that show both relationships.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"defines-engine","label":"Defines an Engine component","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"class\s+Engine\s*:","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"uses-inheritance","label":"Uses inheritance for Car and Vehicle","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"class\s+Car\s*\(\s*Vehicle\s*\)\s*:","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"uses-composition","label":"Stores an Engine inside Car","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"self\s*\.\s*engine\s*=\s*Engine\s*\(\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"prints-result","label":"Prints the relationship checks","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"print\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Inheritance: True
Composition: True
Engine: started</code></pre>","targetSub":"Output showing that a Car is a Vehicle and has an Engine.","files":{"guide":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"# An Engine is a component that another object can contain
class Engine:
    def start(self):
        return "started"

# Vehicle is a general parent class
class Vehicle:
    pass

# Inheritance: Car is a kind of Vehicle
class Car(Vehicle):
    def __init__(self):
        # Composition: Car has an Engine object
        self.engine = Engine()

car = Car()
print("Inheritance:", isinstance(car, Vehicle))
print("Composition:", isinstance(car.engine, Engine))
print("Engine:", car.engine.start())"},"pair":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"class Engine:
