{"title":"Vehicle Motion: Override and Polymorphism","lesson":"L1 · Object-oriented programming 2 · Method override and polymorphism","desc":"Construct a small class hierarchy with a <code>Vehicle</code> base class and <code>Car</code> and <code>Bike</code> subclasses. Override the <code>move()</code> method in each subclass, then use one loop to call <code>move()</code> polymorphically.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"has-vehicle-class","label":"Creates the Vehicle base class","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"class\s+Vehicle\s*:","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"has-car-subclass","label":"Creates Car as a Vehicle subclass","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"class\s+Car\s*\(\s*Vehicle\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"has-bike-subclass","label":"Creates Bike as a Vehicle subclass","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"class\s+Bike\s*\(\s*Vehicle\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"overrides-move","label":"Defines move in the base class and both subclasses","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+move\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":3}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Ruby drives on four wheels
