{"title":"Who Makes That Sound?","lesson":"L1 · Object-Oriented Programming 2 · Method Override and Polymorphism","desc":"Build an <code>Instrument</code> class hierarchy to see polymorphism in action. The inherited <code>concert()</code> method should call <code>self.play()</code>, so Python chooses the version of <code>play()</code> belonging to the actual object. Before running the program, predict which method will print each line.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"has-child-classes","label":"Creates Guitar and Drum child classes","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"class\s+(Guitar|Drum)\s*\(\s*Instrument\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":2},{"id":"overrides-play","label":"Overrides play in the hierarchy","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+play\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":3},{"id":"uses-polymorphic-dispatch","label":"Inherited concert uses self.play","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+concert[\s\S]*?self\.play\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"calls-inherited-method","label":"Calls concert on the objects","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\.concert\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>Guitar: strum
