{"title":"Predict the Click Handler Order","lesson":"L1 · Event-driven programming · Binding handlers","desc":"Complete a small event system and predict the order of three handlers for one <code>click</code> event. Handlers fire in the order they are <em>bound</em>, not the order in which their functions are defined. Record each handler name in <code>fired</code>, trigger the click once, and print the sequence.","startFile":"python","goals":[{"id":"defines-handlers","label":"Defines three event handlers","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"def\s+(show_tip|save_score|play_sound)\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":3},{"id":"records-firing","label":"Records each handler firing","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"fired\s*\.\s*append\s*\(","flags":"i","minCount":3},{"id":"binds-in-order","label":"Binds handlers in the predicted order","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"bind\s*\(\s*["']click["']\s*,\s*play_sound\s*\)[\s\S]*bind\s*\(\s*["']click["']\s*,\s*show_tip\s*\)[\s\S]*bind\s*\(\s*["']click["']\s*,\s*save_score\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1},{"id":"fires-click","label":"Fires the click event once","target":"python","kind":"regex","rule":"\.fire\s*\(\s*["']click["']\s*\)","flags":"i","minCount":1}],"targetHtml":"<pre><code>play_sound -&gt; show_tip -&gt; save_score</code></pre>","targetSub":"The handlers fire in binding order.","files":{"guide":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"class EventSource:
    def __init__(self):
        self.handlers = {}

    def bind(self, event_name, handler):
        if event_name not in self.handlers:
            self.handlers[event_name] = []
        self.handlers[event_name].append(handler)

    def fire(self, event_name):
        for handler in self.handlers.get(event_name, []):
            handler()


fired = []


def show_tip():
    fired.append("show_tip")


def save_score():
    fired.append("save_score")


def play_sound():
    fired.append("play_sound")


button = EventSource()
button.bind("click", play_sound)
button.bind("click", show_tip)
button.bind("click", save_score)

button.fire("click")
print(" -> ".join(fired))"},"pair":{"html":"","css":"","js":"","python":"class EventSource:
